method.description:
Returns [param resource] as text in the format [param format]: [code]&"json"[/code], [code]&"ini"[/code], [code]&"csv"[/code], [code]&"xml"[/code], or a format of a module such as [code]&"toml"[/code] (see [method get_formats]). The text is the same that [ResourceSaver] writes into a file with that extension. See the class description for the [param options]. Returns an empty string and prints an error if the format is unknown or the resource can't be written (for example if it contains itself, or does not fit CSV).
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var compact = ResourceTextSerializer.serialize(settings, &"json", { "indent": "", "enums_as_names": false })
var xml = ResourceTextSerializer.serialize(settings, &"xml")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
string compact = ResourceTextSerializer.Serialize(settings, "json", new Godot.Collections.Dictionary { { "indent", "" }, { "enums_as_names", false } });
string xml = ResourceTextSerializer.Serialize(settings, "xml");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
